---
title: Code lens fixture
---

Prose first, deliberately, so the first runnable cell is not at the top of the
file and an off-by-one in the anchor arithmetic cannot pass by landing on line 0.

Every runnable cell carries `#| cache: false`, which is the one state the lens
labels unconditionally. A fresh cacheable cell is deliberately silent, so without
this the provider would correctly answer nothing and every assertion below would
pass while proving nothing.

```{python}
#| cache: false
a = 1
```

Prose between two runnable cells.

```bash
echo "a plain fence: no braces, so it is not a cell at all"
```

```{bash}
echo "a cell block, but no kernel runs bash, so it earns no button"
```

```{python}
#| cache: false
b = a + 1
```

```python
# a plain highlighted fence, not a cell
print("never executed")
```

```{python}
#| cache: false
z = 2
```
